# 001100-001199/20230508T092610Z_1153786502.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=618b|+GNU diff and git produce "\ No newline at end of file" (or a translated version) as a diagnostic, but this behavior is not portable.<ref>{{cite web %7Ctitle%3DIncomplete Lines (Comparing and Merging Files) %7Curl%3Dhttps://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/manual/html_node/Incomplete%2DLines.html %7Cwebsite%3Dwww.gnu.org}}</ref> GNU patch does not seem to handle this case, while git%2Dapply does.<ref>{{cite web %7Ctitle%3Dgit: apply.c %7Curl%3Dhttps://github.com/git/git/blob/69c786637d7a7fe3b2b8f7d989af095f5f49c3a8/apply.c#LL2901C35%2DL2901C39 %7Cpublisher%3DGit %7Cdate%3D8 May 2023}}</ref>%0A%0A|=23|-1|+doe|=6|-2|+necess|=2|+ily recogniz|=2|+impl|=1|-1|+m|=2|+tation%2Dspecific diff|=2|-1|+utput. GNU|=1|+p|=1|+tch is, however, know|=2|+to recogn|=1|-1|+ze git |=1|+atches and act a litt|=2|-1|+ differ|=3|+ly.<ref>{{cite web %7Ctitle%3Dp|=2|+ch.c\src %2D patch.g|=1|-2|+t %2D GNU patch|=1|+%7Curl%3Dhttp|=1|+://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/|=1|+atch.git/tr|=1|+e/sr|=1|+/patch.c?|=1|+d%3Dc835ecc67b7e37c0d0b7dd7e032209|=1|+daa285808#n1919 %7Cwebs|=1|-1|+te%3Dgit.savannah.gnu.org %7Cquote%3DIn git%2Dstyle|=5|+s,|=1|+the "bef|=1|-1|+re" s|=1|+ate of each |=1|-1|+atch refers to the initial sta|=1|+e before modifying any files,|=1|+.}}</ref>|=3a45|
