# 001100-001199/20230615T043711Z_1160222784.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=5cfc|+%3D%3D%3D Extensions %3D%3D%3D%0AThere are some modifications and extensions to the diff formats that are used and understood by certain programs and in certain contexts. For example, some [[revision control]] systems—such as [[Subversion (software)%7CSubversion]]—specify a version number, "working copy", or any other comment instead of or in addition to a timestamp in the diff's header section.%0A%0ASome tools allow diffs for several different files to be merged into one, using a header for each modified file that may look something like this:%0A%0A Index: path/to/file.cpp%0A%0AThe special case of files that do not end in a newline is not handled. |=1|+either the unidiff utility n|=1|+r|=1|+the POSIX diff standard define a way to handle this type of files. (Indeed, such files are not "text" files by strict POSIX definitions.<ref>http://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/basedefs/V1_chap03.ht|=1|+l#tag_03_403 {{Webarchive%7Curl%3Dhttps://web.archive.|=1|+rg/web/20130429195728/http://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/base|=1|+efs/V1_chap03.html#tag_03_403 %7Cdate%3D2013%2D04%2D29 }} Sect|=1|+on 3.206</re|=1|+>) GNU d|=1|+ff and git produ|=1|+e "\ No newline |=2|+ end of f|=1|+le" (|=1|+r a tra|=2|+lated version) as a diagnostic, but this behavior is not portable.<ref>{{cite web %7Ctitle%3DIncomplete Lines (Comparing and Merging Files) %7Curl%3Dhttps://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/manual/html_node/Incomplete%2DLines.html %7Cwebsite%3Dwww.gnu.org}}</ref> GNU patch does not seem to handle this case, while git%2Dapply does.<ref>{{cite web %7Ctitle%3Dgit: apply.c %7Curl%3Dhttps://github.com/git/git/blob/69c786637d7a7fe3b2b8f7d989af095f5f49c3a8/apply.c#LL2901C35%2DL2901C39 %7Cpublisher%3DGit %7Cdate%3D8 May 2023}}</ref>%0A%0AThe [[Patch (Unix)%7Cpatch]] program does not necessarily recognize implementation%2Dspecific diff output. GNU patch is, however, known to recognize git patches and act a little differently.<ref>{{cite web %7Ctitle%3Dpatch.c\src %2D patch.git %2D GNU patch %7Curl%3Dhttps://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/patch.git/tree/src/patch.c?id%3Dc835ecc67b7e37c0d0b7dd7e032209fdaa285808#n1919 %7Cwebsite%3Dgit.savannah.gnu.org %7Cquote%3DIn git%2Dstyle diffs, the "before" state of each patch refers to the initial state before modifying any files,..}}</ref>|=3bb1|
